[5] The full press conference, which is [available](https://www.facebook.com/RepWilson/videos/2246130255434536/) on Wilson's Facebook page, clarifies who she was referring to in her comments. Around the 9:00 minute mark, someone asks for comment about the border patrol agents involved in the secret Facebook group.

[6] A report from earlier this week [detailed](https://www.propublica.org/article/secret-border-patrol-facebook-group-agents-joke-about-migrant-deaths-post-sexist-memes) how members of the group, which included current and former border patrol agents, joked about migrant deaths "joked about the deaths of migrants, discussed throwing burritos at Latino members of Congress visiting a detention facility in Texas on Monday and posted a vulgar illustration depicting Rep. Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez engaged in oral sex with a detained migrant, according to screenshots of their postings."

[7] Customs and Border Protection has [launched](https://www.npr.org/2019/07/02/737930088/lawmakers-respond-to-vile-secret-facebook-group-created-by-border-patrol-agents) an investigation into the group.

[8] "These posts are completely inappropriate and contrary to the honor and integrity I see—and expect—from our agents day in and day out," Border Patrol Chief Carla Provost said, adding that employees in violation of CBP's conduct standards "will be held accountable."